    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking into some premature longitudinal cracking on a new asphalt section we laid recently here in Phoenix. The weather has been hitting some pretty high temps lately. Can you give me a summary of the primary technical causes for this kind of pavement failure, specifically looking at the relationship between thermal expansion, bitumen viscosity, and subgrade compaction?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
